        "comments": "The assembly cmRicSoro2.1 is based on 51x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and chloroplast genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, the primary assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Order and Orientation of scaffolds on Chromosome 1 between\n9.69-9.94Mb, Chromosome 2 between\n45.63-46.24Mb, Chromosome 3 between\n12.17-12.65Mb and 39.46-39.86Mb, Chromosome 4 between\n17.22-18.20Mb, Chromosome 5 between\n17.96-18.24Mb and Chromosome 8 between\n5.17-5.58Mb is unsure.",
